# This file was empty until now, which meant `git add -A` in a clone of this repo would
# have committed whatever happened to be in the working directory. The three things it
# exists to stop, in order of how much damage they do:
#
#   1. VENDOR DATA. Polygon's terms do not permit redistribution, and the same is true of
#      the Nikkei and soybean sources. download_polygon.py exists precisely so the data
#      never has to be committed. A data folder pushed by accident is a licence breach
#      that is public the moment it lands and stays in the git history after deletion.
#   2. THIRD-PARTY PDFs. The private working tree carries 364 of other people's papers.
#      Publishing them would be copyright infringement at scale.
#   3. SIZE. GitHub rejects any single file over 100MB, and the working tree holds a
#      204MB archive and several 12MB intermediate dumps.

# ---- vendor data: never committed, always downloaded ----
data/

# ---- results: regenerated by a run, and large ----
results/
results_*/
/results*

# ---- the synthetic generator's own marker, if a data dir is ever force-added ----
SYNTHETIC_DATA_DO_NOT_CITE.txt

# ---- third-party papers and the manuscript's build tree ----
Paper/
*.pdf

# ---- backups and pre-edit snapshots ----
*.bak
*.orig
*.prevariants
*.prewriter
*.preregime
*.prefutures
*.prenearby
*.c4bak
*.c5bak
*.c5bak2
*.c7bak

# ---- intermediate binaries and dumps ----
comparison_dictionary*
paired_dict*
six_files_dictionary
outfile_*
write_text*.txt
*.zip

# ---- superseded table pipeline, kept privately ----
# The notebook chain "1 - makemotherfile" -> "2 - log_of_returns" ->
# "3 - table_of_returns" -> "4 - get_table" and its scratch config file
# imported_variables.py are all replaced by make_tables_notebooks.py.
[1-4] *.ipynb
imported_variables.py
main_tables.ipynb
make_tables.py

# ---- superseded engine snapshots and one-off scratch notebooks ----
esp_normal_after_new_signal.py.py
experiment_normal_before_change.py
one_ticker_one_timeformat.ipynb
paperCompare.ipynb
test2.ipynb
test3.ipynb
pygad_test.ipynb

# ---- internal working notes: candid, and not for publication ----
AUDIT_*.md
REVIEW_*.md
PUBLICATION_PLAN.md
VERIFY_THESE.md
chat_transcript.md
problems*.txt
TODO.txt
command_run*.txt
sweep_log.txt
significance_log.txt

# ---- audit artefacts that are evidence, not inputs ----
dividends_2020_2025.csv

# ---- the internal pre-run gate, deliberately NOT published ----
# tests/ is a pre-run gate for the private working tree, not a portable suite. Eight of
# its ten scripts resolve paths as <parent>/Code_1_working/..., one shells out to
# `git show HEAD:Code_1_working/experiment_main.py`, and several assert exact row counts
# and dates of the real vendor data. In a clone of this repository they fail for reasons
# that have nothing to do with the code being wrong, which is worse than their absence.
tests/

# ---- environments and caches ----
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
